Given all inputs and properties tables set-up:
Assume ambient temp is 298K, then T_co = T_amb (non cryogenic)

AREA LOOP (channel area optimization)
Set channel geometry

    PRESSURE LOOP
    Set P_guess

        AXIAL MARCH
        FOR dx in no. geometric stations:
            Calculate flow velocity -> v = mdot / (rho * A)
            Find Reynolds number based on local rho, v, Dh, mu -> Re = rho * v * Dh / mu
            Find Prandtl using local Cp, mu, k -> Pr = Cp * mu / k
            Find Nusselt with Gnielinski
            Find coolant convection HT coeff -> h_c = Nu * k / Dh

            SC HOT WALL TEMP ITERATION
            Set T_hw_guess
            t_hw_converging = False
            WHILE t_hw_converging = False
                Find fin efficiency and correct coolant HT coeff for fins
                Calculate gas convection HT coeff h_g using Bartz and T_hw_guess
                Solve total resistance circuit for heat transfer rate q
                Calculate T_hw from gas-wall convection
                Find error between calculated T_hw and T_hw_guess
                IF abs(error) > tol
                    Update T_hw_guess
                ELSE
                    t_hw_converging = True
            END SC HOT WALL TEMP ITERATION

            Calculate T_cw
            IF coolant is not boiling
                Proceed to CHF CHECK
            ELSE
                Calculate nucleate boiling HT coeff h_nb
                Calculate new nucleate boiling heat transfer rate q_nb
                Calculate T_hw
                Calculate T_cw
                Calculate new T_hw_guess using the converged subcooled T_hw and the new nucleate boiling T_hw

                NB HOT WALL TEMP ITERATION
                t_hw_converging = False
                WHILE t_hw_converging = False
                    Calculate gas convection HT coeff h_g using Bartz and T_hw_guess
                    Calculate nucleate-boiling-corrected coolant convection HT coeff
                    Find fin efficiency and correct coolant HT coeff for fins
                    Solve total resistance circuit for heat transfer rate q
                    Calculate new nucleate boiling HT coeff h_nb for next iteration
                    Find error and update T_hw_guess
                    IF abs(error) > tol
                        Continue iteration
                    ELSE
                        t_hw_converging = True
                END SB HOT WALL TEMP ITERATION

            CHF CHECK
            Calculate wall-coolant heat flux q"
            Find CHF with HH equations and pressure correction
            IF q" >= CHF
                Script fails

            COOLANT UPDATE
            Calculate next T_co from q = mdot * Cp * DeltaT
            Calculate pressure loss through station
                Viscous losses
                    IF laminar -> f = 64 / Re
                    IF turbulent -> solve Colebrook equation for f
                Contraction/Expansion losses
                    Calculate K for expansion or contraction
                Momentum losses
            Update rho with CoolProp
            Update k with CoolProp
            Update Cp with CoolProp
            Update mu with CoolProp

        Exit AXIAL MARCH when all stations are solved

    IF calculated pressure at last station is within tolerance to P_target
        END PRESSURE LOOP
    ELSE
        Calculate new P_guess using secant
        Repeat PRESSURE LOOP

    STRESS ANALYSIS
    IF stress analysis passes and pressure can be optimized further
        Increase channel area
        Repeat AREA LOOP
    ELSE
        Script ends; last run's channel area is final

END AREA LOOP